WEBVTT

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.570
Tomorrow's the last day of summer vacation, huh?

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.500
What should we do tomorrow?

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.530
Do you think you'll finish your homework?

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.220
Yeah, I should be done by tonight, so I'll be free tomorrow.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:23.240
What do you want to do?

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.380
Wanna go somewhere?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.360
That sounds good.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.220
It <i>is</i> the last day, so it'd be nice to go somewhere fun!

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.790
Agreed! Let's have lots and lots of fun!

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:37.800
Yuno—

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.010
cchi...

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.240
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.240
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.570
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.570
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.490
suima ga yatte kite

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.490
When fatigue strikes

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:06.120
atama ga danshingu

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:06.120
My imagination runs wild

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.580
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.580
Everything in life makes me smile

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.420
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.420
Nothing really new takes place

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.050
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.050
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.670
aozora peintingu

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.670
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.720
doko ikou

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.720
Where should we go?

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.300
koko ni iyou

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.300
Let's stay here

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.300
sore wa nani

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.300
What's that?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.890
are yaritai

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.890
I wanna try that!

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.470
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.470
Let's make this moment count

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:29.850
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:29.850
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.520
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.520
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.980
nonbiri na everyday

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.980
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.610
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.610
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.450
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.450
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.030
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.030
So when your heart races in excitement

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.750
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.750
Just draw a sun at the top

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.880
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.880
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.210
gyutto shite ii kana

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.210
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.590
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.590
I've been sketching everything I love

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:05.130
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:05.130
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.890
sore ja ittekimasu

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.890
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.980
"August 31st, The Last Visitor of Summer Break"

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.590
Look at that weather.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:24.330
And it was so nice just yesterday!

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.080
I'll have to cancel all my plans for the day.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.490
Me too.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:32.040
I was gonna have a lot of fun today and make an entry in my picture diary.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.630
It's nice to have something special for the last entry, after all.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.880
Yeah, I'm just keeping them for myself, though.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.210
Looks like we won't even be able to go shopping.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.300
Yeah.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.810
Knowing that I can't go out makes me feel even hungrier.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.190
There's nothing in the fridge right now.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.690
What do we eat for breakfast?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:54.430
What?

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:57.190
We'll have to ask Hiro-san to share.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.280
Yeah.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.070
The wind's too strong!

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:06.830
Yunocchi, be careful.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.610
Oh, Nazuna-sama!

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.530
Nazuna-chan, good morning!

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.790
Where are you going?

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.000
Oh, Yuno-senpai, Miyako-senpai, good morning!

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.720
I didn't have any food,

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.890
so I thought I'd ask Hiro-senpai for some.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.330
Morning!

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.530
Good morning!

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.290
Are you going to Hiro-san too, Nori-chan?

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.020
What?

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.020
How could you tell?!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.530
Jeez...

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.360
You need to remember to always keep some food in the fridge.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.030
Sorry!

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:49.250
What if there was a natural disaster?

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.120
You need to be ready for typhoons like this at the very least.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.500
Is that why you're...

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.080
storing energy down here?

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.340
Hiro-san!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.800
Calm down!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:11.230
The Kanto region showers should be over by early afternoon,

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:15.070
but strong winds will continue past midnight—

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.870
Are you all right, Andou-san?

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.190
Andou-san?!

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.190
She doesn't look like she's having fun.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:21.190
For sure.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.350
Couldn't they have had a stronger guy do the reporting instead?

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:29.580
Sure, but if some big macho man just stood there unmoved by the wind,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.700
and said, "The wind is too strong!",

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.650
it wouldn't really make sense.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:35.830
Macho man?

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:38.590
Oh!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:42.240
The U.S. names their typhoons, don't they?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.800
Oh, you mean hurricanes?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.550
What would be a good name for this typhoon?

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.300
You're gonna name it?

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.920
Like Catherine or Jane?

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.880
Something that captures what makes this typhoon special.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.490
I'm thinking about it.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.310
Hm, then...

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.320
Since she came on the last day of summer vacation,

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.280
how about Summer... Summer...

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.810
Summer Vacation's Lastie.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:05.950
"Lastie"?!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.870
The wind's so strong outside.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:16.110
We were supposed to have so much fun today.

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.040
We'll have to stay home.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.470
Um, I brought trump cards.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.690
If you'd like...

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.070
Oh, Nazuna-san, good job!

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:26.970
Let's play.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.130
Okay!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.470
Hey.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.810
Is your room all right, Miyako?

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:36.430
Huh?

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:40.900
Uh, I mean, with all the rain and wind and stuff...

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.070
Oh!

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:42.650
Yeah.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.530
That's why I'm taking shelter here.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.530
So it's <i>not</i> all right, is it?

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:54.590
What were you gonna do if there was no typhoon?

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:58.090
Well, we didn't really have a plan in mind,

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.690
but since it's the last day of the summer vacation,

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.710
we thought maybe we'd go somewhere really fun.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.390
Right, Yunocchi?

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:07.910
Yeah, so I worked hard to get my homework done.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:10.090
You didn't watch the weather forecast?

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.950
I was busy doing my homework.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:12.680
Here.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.110
I went to bed early last night, so I didn't know.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.050
I didn't watch it either.

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:21.790
I usually just check the weather online.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:26.970
Yesterday, they couldn't say for sure
whether the typhoon would come here.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:29.530
Why did it have to come?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.280
All right.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.050
I'm done!

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.090
Wah, I'm last <i>again</i>?

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:37.700
Yunocchi, hang in there!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:44.470
Today's the last day we can hang out like this on a weekday afternoon, huh?

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.890
We have to go back to school tomorrow, after all.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:50.730
Still, it's been a while since I've seen my classmates.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:51.970
I look forward to seeing them again.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.230
So what should we do about dinner?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.810
I can make some peperoncino.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:09.990
Yay!

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.620
Oh, but I'm out of chili pepper.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.530
Is it okay if it's not spicy?

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:19.730
Oh, I'll go buy some from Berima, then.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:20.830
Nazuna, come with me.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.070
Nori-chan, it's still raining!

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.250
The pasta...

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.590
doesn't have to be perfect.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.670
What are you saying?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.170
It totally does!

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:34.890
"Peperoncino" means "pepper" in the first place!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.810
We can go without it this time.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.020
Yeah.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.070
Okay, eat up.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.280
Let's eat!

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.110
It's so good!

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.570
Hiro-san, you're such a good cook!

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.080
You managed to make it taste amazing even without pepper!

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:00.500
I put in enough garlic to make up for it.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:02.040
What?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:02.830
Huh?

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.130
Tomorrow...

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:10.190
Sorry, everyone, drink some milk!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.470
Coming!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.220
Hello! Anybody order pizza here?

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:22.230
What on earth made you leave your house in <i>this</i> weather?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.650
Well, I was on a delivery, but I thought I'd stop by for a minute.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.870
Is it just me or does this room smell like garlic?

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.870
Oh, sorry.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.990
We're having peperoncino.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.830
Oh, you're eating together?

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:36.990
I like that!

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.950
Oh, looks like you're all doing fine.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.610
Great to see you.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.200
Hello, Landlady!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.620
Good evening!

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.880
Hey, good evening.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.290
Miyako, how's your room?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.040
Oh, yeah.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.460
The water's still leaking a little, but nothing too bad.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:53.850
Thought so.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:56.130
Sorry, I'll get the roof fixed soon.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.050
Okay.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.010
Anyone want some pizza?

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.570
I'll deliver it.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.890
Is it free?

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.850
No way!

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.520
Thought so...

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.130
I'm off, then.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:12.030
Remember to call if you girls need me.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.410
Okay! Thank you very much!

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:15.530
See you!

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.490
All right, catch you later.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.550
Back!

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:29.870
Coming in...

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:36.730
Oh, Miya-chan, before I forget, here!

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:37.720
Your school uniform!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.720
Oh!

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.170
Oh, yeah.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:43.390
It was sent to the cleaners with yours, wasn't it?

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.510
Neat and clean!

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.750
It feels smaller than before.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.060
Huh? Did it shrink?

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:54.070
I had it dry cleaned, though.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.220
I probably just grew bigger.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.170
Oh, right.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:01.200
That's another way to look at it.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:07.210
What's that, Yunocchi?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.550
My personal project for summer vacation.

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:12.880
I thought I'd make the cover before I do today's entry.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.380
Yunocchi, that's great!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.790
Did you separate all the pages?

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.050
Yeah, I took off the spiral.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.680
I'll tie up the pages with strings and glue the cover on.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.030
Got it!

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:26.890
Okay, let's get some fresh air in here.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.140
Wait, Miya-chan!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.140
The wind's still...

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.350
Miya-chan!

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.290
Whoa, Yunocchi, what happened?!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.460
You couldn't see?

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:58.260
When I began, I could only think about how much I had to do,

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.830
but now it feels like everything went by in a flash.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:01.550
Yeah.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.800
But we still did a lot of things.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:04.970
Yeah!

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.510
It was a fun summer vacation.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:08.470
Yep!

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:10.020
Huh?

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:12.130
I'm missing entries for two of the days.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.690
Where did they go?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.690
Maybe you forgot to draw them?

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:17.610
I gathered all the pages, didn't I?

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.230
Yeah.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.990
Well, this is for myself anyway.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.550
Yay!

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:27.740
Yay...?

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:37.510
I ran into a lot of trouble today.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:43.510
But it was fun eating, playing cards, and chatting with everyone.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.780
It's great out today!

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:05.700
Hiro-san, Sae-san, good morning!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.200
Morning!

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.990
Good morning!

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.570
Morning!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.500
The new semester starts today!

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.330
Let's make it a good one!

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:15.830
Of course!

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.830
September 1st, The 5 D's

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.340
Yuno-san! Miyako!

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.840
It's been a while!

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.850
Morning! It's great to see you again!

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.010
Morning!

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.650
Yesterday's typhoon was something else.

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:32.270
Yeah, it was.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.520
I didn't manage to get my shopping done.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.520
It might be because the typhoon passed by,

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.930
but it's a really hot day for September.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:41.900
There's still a lot of lingering summer heat.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:46.400
It's so cool here!

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:49.570
This is one of the reasons I love going to a private school.

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:53.050
Yeah, it's pretty nice to have air-conditioned classrooms.

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:53.910
Yep.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:57.500
I used to go to public school, and it got so hot during class!

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.850
This place might be more expensive, but it's nicer too.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:01.540
That's a private school for you!

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:05.010
Let's get the open ceremony started.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.760
First up, we have the principal's speech.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:17.520
Private school...

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.610
Good morning, everyone!

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.980
I'm looking forward to working with you for the second semester.

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:28.330
Try your best to cherish and enjoy each of your days here.

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:33.740
If you can do that, you'll find the semester much more fun and fulfilling!

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.690
That's a great piece of advice.

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.870
Yeah, it's wonderful.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:41.370
What she's <i>saying</i> is certainly good.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:46.130
There will be an emergency drill soon.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.510
To simulate a real emergency, the exact time of the drill is unknown,

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.260
so you have free time until then.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.260
Oh, but don't leave the classroom, okay?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:14:00.130
So, Yunocchi, why don't you show her your project now?

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.610
Huh? I didn't bring it with me.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.770
You're not gonna show it to her?

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:07.860
Well, it was my personal project.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:12.230
I'd be too embarrassed to share it.

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:16.290
But I guess being the shy one <i>and</i> the artist is who you are.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.160
It's time.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:21.430
Attention, a magnitude 6.0
earthquake has just occurred,

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:23.670
and a fire has broken out in the home economics classroom.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:27.420
Students, please follow your teacher's instructions

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.050
and evacuate via the west
stairwell in a timely manner.

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:37.430
Sensei, aren't we going to evacuate?

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:42.710
I wonder why someone was in the home-ec room on opening ceremony day.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:45.270
Will we make it out in time?

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:51.280
Stay low and cover your mouth with a handkerchief as you evacuate!

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.530
Handkerchief, handkerchief.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.150
Miya-chan, you don't have a handkerchief?

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:56.910
Huh?

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.540
I don't, but it's all right.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.210
M-Miya-chan...

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.850
It looks like that cami-whatever it's called, doesn't it?

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:10.090
No, not at all!

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.710
What are they doing?

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:34.200
Is that how they talk?

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:43.410
Nazuna!

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.870
What are you doing?

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:47.110
The regular division is already all going!

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:48.500
Oh, Nori-chan.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:52.720
I have to go to the restroom.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:53.630
What?!

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:56.470
The school is on fire!

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.930
Hold it until we've evacuated!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.260
B-But...

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:02.810
I don't know when I'll be able to go if I don't go now.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.520
But the more important thing

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.190
is to get out of the school building first!

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.610
Nori-chan, are you gonna take responsibility?

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.150
I have no idea what you mean.

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:19.930
It took eight minutes to complete the evacuation and start the roll call.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:23.430
We can't say that it was very fast,

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:29.350
but you did seem to line up and start the roll call fast on the schoolyard.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:33.880
It wasn't good that the line was congested on the stairs.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:38.460
Second and third-year students be more considerate

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:41.720
of the first-years on the fourth floor and move more swiftly and calmly.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:46.340
Let's do better so we don't have to ever use this.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:49.610
Does he like high places?

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:53.150
Hey, Yunocchi, doesn't it hurt to crouch like that?

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:53.900
Huh?

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:56.590
I don't want to get my skirt dirty, though.

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:58.450
Everyone else is keeping their butts off the ground too.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.450
You can just dust it off afterward.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:01.390
There.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.250
Whoa, I'm sorry!

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.250
Wow, it's so hot!

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:17.210
People might start getting sick in this heat.

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:19.720
Yeah, that does happen at morning meetings from time to time.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:21.800
Nori-chan...

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:29.940
S-Sensei, I'm not feeling too well.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.610
It's hot today, after all.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.730
<i>Thank you!</i>

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:40.490
Thanks to the cooperation of the Asagi Fire Department,

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:43.490
we have an earthquake simulator today!

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:49.810
I hope this shows you all how
frightening earthquakes can be.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.400
All right, Yuno-san.

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:53.840
Come try it!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.090
What? Why me?!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.100
Okay!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.310
Do you have a better sense of how scary earthquakes are now?

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:10.190
Sure we do!

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.830
School's out!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.970
Let's hurry home.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:23.870
My legs are starting to hurt after all that squatting.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.410
Nori-chan, thanks for earlier.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.230
Huh?

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.270
Did I do something to deserve thanks?

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.030
You know it, Nori-chan.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:38.710
Yuno-san, the earthquake simulation was something else, wasn't it?

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:39.670
Yeah.

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:41.850
It was tough, but you did great, Yunocchi.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:44.140
Thank you, Miya-chan.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:48.050
Hey, do you remember the Three D's from elementary school?

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:50.680
You know, like, "Don't push, don't run, don't talk."

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:52.270
Oh, that!

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:55.530
My school had four.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:57.480
We also had, "Don't go back."

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:02.590
My school had, "Don't get close,"
on top of that, making it the Five D's.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:04.490
There's more than one version, huh?

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:06.950
Hey, guys....

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:10.700
Why don't we get some red bean paste and soy flour, and make mochi for snacks?

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.880
We're in!

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:19.880
Let's eat!

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:25.090
It's so hot! But it's so good!

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:29.330
Yamabuki High is amazing in many ways.

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:32.490
Like how they had a hook-and-ladder truck and an earthquake simulator.

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:34.350
Yeah, that frightened me for a second.

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:35.530
Don't worry.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:37.980
You're not the only one that was frightened.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:40.980
Yeah, we didn't have them last year.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.030
That's a private school for you!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.780
What? You think that's the reason?

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:48.230
Classes start tomorrow, don't they?

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:50.620
Yeah. The school cafeteria too.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:53.910
I need to think about what to get for lunch tomorrow!

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.790
You never change, Miya-chan.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:00.650
Hey, Sae, do you want to go to Berima with me later?

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:03.530
I'm out of food, so I need to go buy some more.

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:04.880
Yeah, sure.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:06.750
Me too.

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:08.030
Do you wanna go too, Miya-chan?

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:09.560
Yeah, I'll go.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.170
Oh, I'll join too.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.970
Sorry about that.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:16.060
Sorry.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.900
Me too.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.550
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:22.650
That's what it's there for!

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.970
Let's all go together later.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:25.820
Okay!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.390
Can I come too?

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:29.610
Of course!

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:33.120
All right, let's finish the mochi.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.250
Okay!

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:40.090
So here you were, Yoshinoya-sensei.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:41.890
Principal!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:44.170
What are you up to?

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:45.930
I'm cleaning the supplies.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.970
I just finished.

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.450
I rarely use mine during class,

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:54.480
but I thought I'd clean them for the new semester.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:57.020
How admirable.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:01.230
Anyway, did you need something from me, Principal?

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:04.670
I'm thinking about holding a faculty dinner.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:05.740
What do you say?

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:06.950
Oh?

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:09.010
Since we have a new semester ahead of us,

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:13.580
it'll be a good opportunity for the faculty to get closer as they work hard for education.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.080
Okay!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:18.010
There'll be no alcohol, though,

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:19.670
since there are classes tomorrow.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:20.670
Okay.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.960
Please get changed then.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:26.880
No "okay" this time?

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:39.290
So many things have happened these past two days.

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:44.440
There was a typhoon, and I had to go into an earthquake simulator.

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:48.950
Oh yeah, I should draw what happened today in my sketchbook!

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:54.490
Well, I don't need a personal project anymore.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:01.570
Since it's just a personal project, all I have to do is keep drawing when I want to, right?

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:03.420
Yeah, I'll do that.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:06.170
I'll work hard for the second semester too!

00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:13.920
It's time for the Hidamari meeting.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:15.780
Today's subect is the swimming competition!

00:22:15.780 --> 00:22:17.480
I'm making lunches for everyone!

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:20.400
Oh, yeah! Please put extra meat in mine!

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:21.660
More fruits for me!

00:22:21.660 --> 00:22:23.120
Cool barley tea, too!

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:24.640
We're not here to talk about food!

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:25.060
Huh?

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:26.060
We're not?

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:28.200
We were supposed to discuss strategy.

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:34.180
Next time: "September 15th, The Photo
Opportunity of Victory! Miyako Will Win!"

00:22:34.180 --> 00:22:37.900
We'll be waiting at Yamabuki High School. Please come see us!
